# Installed Loom surfaces hand-patched locally — resync must not clobber.
#
# scripts/generate-agents-md.sh: upstream template resolves SRC/DEFAULT_OUT as
# $SCRIPT_DIR/../.loom/…, which assumes the Loom source layout
# (defaults/scripts/ next to defaults/.loom/) and breaks in this flattened
# install (.loom/scripts/ next to .loom/CLAUDE.md) with "source not found".
# Local two-line fix per docs/decisions/PDR-0001-generate-agents-md-path-fix.md.
# The same entry's local delta also covers the {{INSTALL_DATE}} substitution
# (#533): the generator resolves the placeholder itself from
# .loom/install-metadata.json (mirroring resync-installed.sh) and refuses to
# emit any surviving placeholder, because .loom/AGENTS.md here is the
# already-substituted artifact, not the installer's template. Same upstream
# thread: rjwalters/loom#13910 (second gap; appending it there is an
# operator-only follow-up — this repo's credentials cannot post upstream).
#
# Third local delta under the same pin (#640): the write path copies the
# existing target's mode onto the mktemp'd render before the mv (else 644),
# because mktemp's 0600 tightened .loom/AGENTS.md to owner-only on every
# regeneration. Same upstream thread: rjwalters/loom#13910.
#
# Permanent pin: this script is repo-owned, not a hold awaiting an upstream
# fix. Upstream retired the installed generator (rjwalters/loom#13911,
# 2026-11-17) — deleted from defaults/ and declared in
# defaults/.loom-retired.list — so no resync has an upstream file left to
# install. A layout-aware path fix did land upstream (7a424b723), but the
# generator stopped shipping to consumers the same day (a52433957); the copy
# still in the Loom repo at scripts/ is source-tree-only and never ships. The
# #13910 follow-up noted above is therefore moot for this install.
#
# Do not remove the pin line. It is what stops remove_retired_files() in
# resync-installed.sh from deleting the script as retired payload — the daemon
# resync's retired-payload sweep honors the same pin, per that script's header
# — and CI runs tools/test_generate_agents_md.py against it. The pin ends
# only if this repo itself deletes or relocates the script, never by a
# resync. So `resync-pin status` reporting "file REMOVED upstream" is the
# steady state here, not a dead pin. Record: PDR-0001, 2026-11-28 update
# (path above).
scripts/generate-agents-md.sh
